@@ -40,0 +41,5 @@
+This branch's clean HUD rearranges speed, set speed, slowdown reasons and enforcement information, with a two-rail path and 3D surrounding cars. The 3D view labels the lead and cut-in vehicles while hiding individual radar points and the lower system-status line. Surrounding car shapes are selected by track ID, not by recognizing their actual make or model.
+
+The ego car uses the detected Ioniq 5, EV9, fourth-generation Carnival, Staria or Tucson, or fifth-generation Sportage model. Missing or failed models fall back to the EV6. While onroad, P prioritizes the selected car, clock, tyre pressures, trip statistics and available vehicle-decoded battery level. R prioritizes the same car with a steering-based path and blind-spot warnings. The reverse guide is an illustrative EV6-geometry reference. Other gears restore the selected HUD mode.
+
+Parking weather queries Open-Meteo using the last GPS position rounded to approximately 1 km, with a cache age of up to one hour. Create `/data/ev6_weather_off` to disable fetching. `/data/ev6_hud_classic` disables the clean layout and P/R screens; `/data/ev6_device_screen_on` disables automatic device-screen sleep. Vehicle model selection is independent of these files.
